# Renderer Theme And Styling

- Prefer semantic theme tokens over raw colors. Add or adjust tokens in `src/renderer/styles/globals.css` and expose them through `tailwind.config.js` before using new visual values in components.
- Use the existing theme system (`dark` / `light`, CSS variables, semantic Tailwind aliases like `bg-bg`, `text-text`, `border-border`) instead of hardcoded hex values.
- Keep `src/renderer/lib/theme.tsx` responsible for theme selection and persistence, not component-level styling decisions.
- Reuse helper classes like `btn-*`, `glass`, `card`, `hover-overlay`, and semantic status colors where possible before inventing one-off styles.
- When adding UI states, check both themes for readable contrast and consistent behavior.
